# WN22-CC-000380: Windows Server 2022 Remote Desktop Services must be configured with the client connection encryption set to High Level.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-cc-000380-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Remote Desktop Services must be configured with the client connection encryption set to High Level.`
    description `Remote connections must be encrypted to prevent interception of data or sensitive information. Selecting "High Level" will ensure encryption of Remote Desktop Services sessions in both directions. Satisfies: SRG-OS-000033-GPOS-00014, SRG-OS-000250-GPOS-00093`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium,ksi-iam-elp,ksi-svc-asm,ksi-svc-snt`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-ELP,KSI:KSI-SVC-ASM,KSI:KSI-SVC-SNT,NIST-800-53:AC-17(2)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-ELP,KSI-SVC-ASM,KSI-SVC-SNT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> Remote Desktop Services >> Remote Desktop Session Host >> Security >> Set client connection encryption level to "Enabled" with "High Level" selected.`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_IAM_ELP `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-ELP by setting registry value 'MinEncryptionLevel' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows NT\Terminal Services' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_ASM `Windows Server implements KSI-SVC-ASM by setting registry value 'MinEncryptionLevel' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows NT\Terminal Services' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_SNT `Windows Server implements KSI-SVC-SNT by setting registry value 'MinEncryptionLevel' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows NT\Terminal Services' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_AC_17_2 `Windows Server implements AC-17(2) by setting registry value 'MinEncryptionLevel' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows NT\Terminal Services' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows NT\Terminal Services`
        name `MinEncryptionLevel`
        behavior executor powershell
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 3
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
